#%PAM-1.0
# PAM service for qypr-lock password unlock.
#
# Installed as /etc/pam.d/qypr-lock. When present, the lock screen checks the
# typed password against this stack instead of "login" (see
# PamAuthenticator::passwordService()).
#
# Why not "login": fingerprint setups commonly put `auth sufficient
# pam_fprintd.so` at the top of the login stack (on Arch, in
# /etc/pam.d/system-local-login). PAM runs modules in order, so a typed
# password would wait behind a fingerprint scan ("Place your finger on the
# reader") for up to the fprintd timeout, and that scan would fight the
# parallel qypr-fingerprint worker for the reader. Keeping pam_fprintd out of
# this stack is what lets either the password or a finger unlock on its own.
#
# Keep it that way: do NOT add pam_fprintd.so here (or to the stacks this
# includes). Fingerprint lives in /etc/pam.d/qypr-fingerprint.
auth      include   system-auth
# Parity with "login": re-unlock the GNOME keyring with the typed password if
# it was locked. The leading '-' skips it silently where it is not installed.
-auth     optional  pam_gnome_keyring.so
account   include   system-auth
